.DS_Store

# The Android project IS committed: it carries the app icons, versioning and the
# release signing wiring, which `npx cap add` would not regenerate. Only its build
# output and machine-local paths are ignored. iOS is still generated on a Mac.
# The iOS project is TRACKED, like android/ is — ios.yml only runs `cap sync ios`,
# which syncs an existing platform rather than creating one, so ignoring the whole
# directory meant CI checked out a tree with no iOS project to build. That is why the
# workflow never produced anything. Only the generated and per-developer parts are
# ignored below.
/ios/App/Pods/
/ios/App/build/
/ios/App/App/public/
/ios/capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins/
/ios/App/App.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
/ios/App/App.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
/ios/App/App.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
/ios/DerivedData/
/android/build/
/android/app/build/
/android/.gradle/
/android/local.properties
/android/app/src/main/assets/public/
/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
/android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
.gradle/

# Release signing material — never commit a keystore or its passwords.
*.jks
*.keystore
signing.properties
release-artifacts/
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/

# Generated by scripts/build-engine.sh from the built engine library on every build.
# Tracking it meant a clone could compile against a binding that no longer matched the
# library — it sat here from 27 September while the engine gained three functions, and a
# build that skipped build-engine.sh silently used the old one.
android/app/src/main/java/uniffi/
.engine-bindings/
